ere are two problems with the packet itself:\n- `<samples-dir>` is a placeholder that was never replaced with a real path, and the shell reads `<` as \"take input from a file called samples-dir\".\n- `.theseus/oracle/perf/profile-fonts.js` doesn't exist on this branch.\n\nPKT-0083, the packet that fixes this acceptance line, is still in `pending`.\n\n**Code change.** This is unchanged from attempt 1 and is commit `f11c1d1` on branch `pkt/PKT-0081` in the `external/sdkjs` clone. That directory isn't tracked by this repository, so the fork still needs to be pushed. The change adds a bounded cache (200k entries) to `StringRender.js` that remembers the result of `FragmentShaper.shapeFragment` for each font, size, style, PPI and text. Cells whose text and font didn't change no longer get re-shaped by HarfBuzz. The cache returns the same widths the shaper would compute, so wrapping and bidi should be unaffected. That is only by reasoning: I checked the syntax, but I haven't built sdkjs or run a profile, so I have no timing or `HB_ShapeText` counts.\n\n**What I committed this time.**\n- `57c19c0`: a note in the Executor log for attempt 3.\n- `df3c8ff`: the friction line. My first version was in the wrong format and `theseus validate` rejected it; the fix passes (0 errors, plus the usual pilot-mode warning).\n- I didn't open a new follow-up request, because PKT-0083 already covers the fix.\n\n**What the factory needs to do.** This was the last allowed attempt (`max_attempts: 3`). To make the packet passable, add `depends_on: [PKT-0083]`, replace `<samples-dir>` with a real path, make sure `profile-fonts.js` is on the base branch, and then re-queue it.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas.**\n- On spreadsheet remote apply, the shaping cost comes from how many times `shapeFragment` is called, not from each call being slow. Caching by font, PPI and text removes the repeat calls.\n- Placeholders like `<samples-dir>` in acceptance commands need to be resolved before a packet is queued.\n-